## Control {{controlId}}: Limit System Access to Authorized Users

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization limits information system access to authorized users through role-based access control (RBAC) implemented via Azure Active Directory security groups and Conditional Access policies within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant.

{{#if cuiGroupExists}}
The "{{groupDisplayName}}" security group ({{memberCount}} members) defines the authorized user population for CUI access. Group membership is managed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}} and reviewed quarterly per procedure AC-001.
{{else}}
CUI-Authorized-Users security group has not been created. Access control relies on manual authorization processes pending automation implementation.
{{/if}}

{{#if policies}}
Access enforcement is automated via the following Conditional Access policies:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Requires {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}{{#if grantControls.authenticationStrength}} with {{grantControls.authenticationStrength}} authentication strength{{/if}}. Applied to {{conditions.users}} users and {{conditions.applications}} applications.
{{/each}}
{{else}}
Conditional Access policies have not been configured. Access restrictions are enforced via Azure AD group membership only.
{{/if}}

{{#if infraResources}}
Supporting infrastructure resources:
{{#each infraResources}}
- {{resourceType}} "{{name}}"{{#if properties.retention_days}} (retention: {{properties.retention_days}} days){{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine Azure AD group membership reports, Conditional Access policy configurations, and quarterly access review logs.

